NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001083 "alignment of cells. Override table argument and per-row attribute of the same"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001084 "name, but is overridden by per-cell attribute of the same name."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001085 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001086 "=item * valign"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001087 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001088 "String. Value is either C<\"top\">, C<\"middle\">, C<\"bottom\">. Specify vertical"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001089 "text alignment of cells. Override table argument and per-row attribute of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001090 "same name, but is overridden by per-cell attribute of the same name."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001091 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001092 "=item * lpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001093 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001094 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001095 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001096 "=item * rpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001097 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001098 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001099 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001100 "=item * hpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001101 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001102 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001103 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001104 "=item * tpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001105 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001106 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001107 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001108 "=item * bpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001109 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001110 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001111 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001112 "=item * vpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001113 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001114 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001115 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001116 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001117 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001118 "=head1 PER-CELL ATTRIBUTES"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001119 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001120 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001121 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001122 "=item * align"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001123 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001124 "String. Value is either C<\"left\">, C<\"middle\">, C<\"right\">. Override table"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001125 "argument, per-row attribute, and per-column attribute of the same name."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001126 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001127 "=item * valign"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001128 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001129 "String. Value is either C<\"top\">, C<\"middle\">, C<\"bottom\">. Specify vertical"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001130 "text alignment of cells. Override table argument, per-row attribute, and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001131 "per-column attribute of the same name."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001132 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001133 "=item * colspan"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001134 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001135 "Positive integer. Default 1."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001136 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001137 "=item * rowspan"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001138 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001139 "Positive integer. Default 1."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001140 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001141 "=item * bottom_border."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001142 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001143 "Boolean. Currently the attribute of he leftmost cell is used."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001144 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001145 "=item * top_border."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001146 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001147 "Boolean. Currently the attribute of he leftmost cell is used."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001148 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001149 "=item * lpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001150 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001151 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001152 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001153 "=item * rpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001154 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001155 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001156 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001157 "=item * hpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001158 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001159 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001160 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001161 "=item * tpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001162 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001163 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001164 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001165 "=item * bpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001166 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001167 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001168 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001169 "=item * vpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001170 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001171 "Integer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001172 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001173 "=item * pad_char"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001174 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001175 "String."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001176 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001177 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001178 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001179 "=head1 FUNCTIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001180 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001181 "=head2 generate_table"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001182 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001183 "Usage:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001184 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001185 " my $table_str = generate_table(%args);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001186 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001187 "Arguments:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001188 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001189 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001190 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001191 "=item * rows"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001192 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001193 "Array of arrayrefs (of strings or hashrefs). Required. Each array element is a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001194 "row of cells. A cell can be a string like C<\"foo\"> specifying only the text"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001195 "(equivalent to C<< {text=>\"foo\"} >>) or a hashref which allows you to specify a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001196 "cell's text (C<text>) as well as attributes like C<rowspan> (int, >= 1),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001197 "C<colspan> (int, >= 1), etc. See L</PER-CELL ATTRIBUTES> for the list of known"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001198 "per-cell attributes."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001199 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001200 "Currently, C<top_border> and C<bottom_border> needs to be specified for the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001201 "first column of a row and will take effect for the whole row."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001202 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001203 "Alternatively, you can also specify cell attributes using L</cell_attrs>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001204 "argument."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001205 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001206 "=item * header_row"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001207 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001208 "Int. Optional. Default 0. Number of rows that are header. Note that in"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001209 "Text::Table::Tiny, this option is a boolean. We use integer to support multirow"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001210 "header."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001211 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001212 "=item * border_style"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001213 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001214 "Str. Optional. Uses default from the environment variable"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001215 "L</PERL_TEXT_TABLE_MORE_BORDER_STYLE>, or environment variable L</BORDER_STYLE>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001216 "or C<ASCII::SingleLineDoubleAfterHeader>. This is Perl module under the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001217 "L<BorderStyle> namespace, without the namespace prefix. To see how a border"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001218 "style looks like, you can use the CLI L<show-border-style> from"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001219 "L<App::BorderStyleUtils>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001220 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001221 "=item * align"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001222 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001223 "String. Value is either C<\"left\">, C<\"middle\">, C<\"right\">. Specify horizontal"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001224 "text alignment of cells. Overriden by overridden by per-row, per-column, or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001225 "per-cell attribute of the same name."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001226 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001227 "=item * valign"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001228 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001229 "String. Value is either C<\"top\">, C<\"middle\">, C<\"bottom\">. Specify vertical"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001230 "text alignment of cells. Overriden by overridden by per-row, per-column, or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001231 "per-cell attribute of the same name."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001232 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001233 "=item * row_attrs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001234 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001235 "Array of records. Optional. Specify per-row attributes. Each record is a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001236 "2-element arrayref: C<< [$row_idx, \\%attrs] >>. C<$row_idx> is zero-based. See"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001237 "L</PER-ROW ATTRIBUTES> for the list of known attributes."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001238 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001239 "=item * col_attrs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001240 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001241 "Array of records. Optional. Specify per-column attributes. Each record is a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001242 "2-element arrayref: C<< [$col_idx, \\%attrs] >>. C<$col_idx> is zero-based. See"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001243 "L</PER-COLUMN ATTRIBUTES> for the list of known attributes."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001244 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001245 "=item * cell_attrs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001246 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001247 "Array of records. Optional. Specify per-cell attributes. Each record is a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001248 "3-element arrayref: C<< [$row_idx, $col_idx, \\%attrs] >>. C<$row_idx> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001249 "C<$col_idx> are zero-based. See L</PER-CELL ATTRIBUTES> for the list of known"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001250 "attributes."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001251 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001252 "Alternatively, you can specify a cell's attribute in the L</rows> argument"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001253 "directly, by specifying a cell as hashref."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001254 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001255 "=item * lpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001256 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001257 "Integer. Optional. Set number of padding characters to add at the left side of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001258 "table cells. Overrides C<hpad>. Overridden by per-row/per-column/per-cell"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001259 "padding attributes. See also C<rpad>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001260 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001261 "=item * rpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001262 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001263 "Integer. Optional. Set number of padding characters to add at the right side of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001264 "table cells. Overrides C<hpad>. Overridden by per-row/per-column/per-cell"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001265 "padding attributes. See also C<rpad>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001266 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001267 "=item * hpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001268 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001269 "Integer. Optional. Set number of padding characters to add at the left and right"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001270 "sides of table cells. Overridden by C<lpad> for left side, and C<rpad> for right"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001271 "side. Overridden by per-row/per-column/per-cell padding attributes. See also"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001272 "C<vpad>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001273 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001274 "Default is 1."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001275 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001276 "=item * tpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001277 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001278 "Integer. Optional. Set number of padding lines to add at the top side of table"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001279 "cells. Overrides C<vpad>. Overridden by per-row/per-column/per-cell padding"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001280 "attributes. See also C<bpad>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001281 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001282 "=item * bpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001283 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001284 "Integer. Optional. Set number of padding lines to add at the bottom side of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001285 "table cells. Overrides C<vpad>. Overridden by per-row/per-column/per-cell"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001286 "padding attributes. See also C<tpad>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001287 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001288 "=item * vpad"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001289 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001290 "Integer. Optional. Set number of padding lines to add at the top and bottom"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001291 "sides of table cells. Overridden by C<tpad> for top side, and C<bpad> for bottom"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001292 "side. Overridden by per-row/per-column/per-cell padding attributes. See also"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001293 "C<hpad>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001294 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001295 "Default is 0."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001296 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001297 "=item * pad_char"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001298 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001299 "String. Optional. Must be one character long. Default is C< > (space character)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001300 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001301 "=item * separate_rows"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001302 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001303 "Boolean. Optional. Default 0. If set to true, will add a separator between data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001304 "rows. Equivalent to setting C<bottom_border> or C<top_border> attribute to true"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001305 "for each row."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001306 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001307 "=item * wide_char"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001308 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001309 "Boolean. Optional. Default false. Turn on wide character support. Cells that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001310 "contain wide Unicode characters will still be properly aligned. Note that this"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001311 "requires optional prereq L<Text::WideChar::Util> or L<Text::ANSI::WideUtil>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001312 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001313 "=item * color"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001314 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001315 "Boolean. Optional. Default false. Turn on color support. Cells that contain ANSI"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001316 "color codes will still be properly aligned. Note that this requires optional"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001317 "prereq L<Text::ANSI::Util> or L<Text::ANSI::WideUtil>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001318 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001319 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001320 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001321 "=head1 FAQ"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001322 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001323 "=head2 Can I have multiple header rows?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001324 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001325 "Yes, by setting L</header_row> option to 2 or whatever number of header rows you"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001326 "have. See example script F<multirow-header.pl> in this distribution."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001327 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001328 "=head1 ENVIRONMENT"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001329 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001330 "=head2 PERL_TEXT_TABLE_MORE_BORDER_STYLE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001331 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001332 "String. Used to set the default for the L</border_style> option. Has higher"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001333 "precedence than L</BORDER_STYLE>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001334 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001335 "=head2 BORDER_STYLE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001336 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001337 "String. Used to set the default for the L</border_style> option. Has lower"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001338 "precedence than L</PERL_TEXT_TABLE_MORE_BORDER_STYLE>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001339 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001340 "=head1 HOMEPAGE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001341 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001342 "Please visit the project's homepage at L<https://metacpan.org/release/Text-Table-More>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001343 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001344 "=head1 SOURCE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001345 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001346 "Source repository is at L<https://github.com/perlancar/perl-Text-Table-More>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001347 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001348 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001349 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001350 "L<Text::ANSITable> also offers lots of formatting options, but currently lacks"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001351 "support for rowspan/colspan. It also uses an OO interface and has features I"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001352 "never use: hiding rows and selecting display columns different from declared"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001353 "columns. I currently plan to actively develop Text::Table::More instead of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001354 "Text::ANSITable, but we'll see."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001355 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001356 "L<Acme::CPANModules::TextTable> contains a comparison and benchmark for modules"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001357 "that generate text table."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001358 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001359 "HTML E<lt>TABLEE<gt> element,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001360 "L<https://www.w3.org/TR/2014/REC-html5-20141028/tabular-data.html>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001361 "L<https://www.w3.org/html/wiki/Elements/table>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001362 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001363 "=head1 AUTHOR"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001364 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001365 "perlancar <perlancar@cpan.org>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001366 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001367 "=head1 CONTRIBUTING"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001368 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001369 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001370 "To contribute, you can send patches by email/via RT, or send pull requests on"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001371 "GitHub."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001372 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001373 "Most of the time, you don't need to build the distribution yourself. You can"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001374 "simply modify the code, then test via:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001375 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001376 " % prove -l"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001377 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001378 "If you want to build the distribution (e.g. to try to install it locally on your"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001379 "system), you can install L<Dist::Zilla>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001380 "L<Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::PERLANCAR>, and sometimes one or two other"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001381 "Dist::Zilla plugin and/or Pod::Weaver::Plugin. Any additional steps required"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001382 "beyond that are considered a bug and can be reported to me."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001383 ""
